    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Those are great examples. Just to help my students understand the weight of these decisions, how would you describe the impact of these rulings on society? Like, why is it so important that the court uses substantive due process to safeguard these rights instead of just sticking to narrow procedural rules?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Rulings based on substantive due process force the government to respect the fundamental moral and liberty interests of the individual, going beyond just checking legal boxes. This is vital because often, a law can be perfectly \"procedural\" (a clear rule of law) but still be deeply oppressive or violate essential human rights. By using this doctrine, the Supreme Court acts as a necessary check, ensuring the Constitution is not just a set of rules for government, but a robust guarantee of personal freedom for *all* citizens.",
      "source": "target",
